  sha256 before: 3c1b6ff9aa60fdf720ab73f8cdcdd647841eb3a266cfc1263a300664dd9a3fae
  sha256 after:  c3942019f6122ed0733b7fe19e80ded6a2113f3e8f124a408e8c2e65da997690

Playwright is Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation and licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0: see LICENSE-Apache-2.0.txt and NOTICE-playwright.txt next
to this file. The hunks below state every change made for the Ouroboros
chrome_browser skill (Ouroboros contributors, 2026). The skill applies them in
memory when its server starts; the installed package files are not modified.

What changes, by hunk:
  1-5  Pointer actions: an optional hook (off unless the skill installs it)
       replaces the page's requestAnimationFrame "stable" wait with host-timed
       sampling, and records whether a trusted event reached the target.
       Visible, enabled, non-inert and hit-target checks are unchanged, and the
       states are still read after the target has settled.
  6    Request interception: the real CORS preflight is continued instead of
       being answered with a permissive 204.
  7-8  MCP tabs: tabs the agent opens are marked; selecting a tab does not bring
       it to front; a lost or crashed tab is never replaced by a new one; only
       tabs the agent opened can be closed.
  9    Extension relay: new tabs are created with active:false.
  10-11 Extension relay: no token or protocol override from the environment;
       the connect-page URL is returned to the caller instead of a browser being
       located and spawned with it.
  12-13 Browser factories: profile discovery, launching and attaching are
       disabled; the skill connects only through its own browser_connect.
  14   Exports: the relay class and the hook setter for the skill adapter.

